Consider a 'users' collection and an 'orders' collection. You execute the following aggregation pipeline stage on 'users':

{
  "$lookup": {
    "from": "orders",
    "localField": "_id",
    "foreignField": "userId",
    "as": "userOrders"
  }
}

If a user document with `_id: 101` exists in 'users' but has no corresponding documents in 'orders', what will be the value of the `userOrders` field in the resulting document for that user?

You are analyzing an aggregation pipeline stage defined as follows:

{
  "$group": {
    "_id": "$department",
    "totalSalary": { "$sum": "$salary" },
    "employeeList": { "$push": "$name" }
  }
}

Which statement correctly describes the behavior of this stage?
